tip: | Look at the rock. | No face of it lines up with the grid, but it is still a top, a lit side and a shaded side.
tip: 3 | Think in flat planes. | Four values, each a flat shape with straight edges. Curves make a rock look soft; corners make it hard.
tip: | Try it. | Cracks go where two planes meet. Add a dark line along one edge with the Pencil and the rock gets harder. | pencil
